<title>SWEDEN: Skandia, Stadshypotek to merge.</title>
<headline>Skandia, Stadshypotek to merge.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurance company Skandia and mortgage bank Stadshypotek said they will merge to become the leading financial institution in the Nordic region.  </p>
<p>The new group, to be called Skandia Stadshypotek, will have total assets of about 500 billion crowns ($75.3 billion), net assets of 37.5 billion and a total market capitalisation of about 45 billion as at November 22.</p>
<p>The merger will be effected by an offer to the shareholders in Stadshypotek to exchange their shares for newly issued shares in Skandia.</p>
<p>Voting restrictions in Skandia's articles of association are expected to be removed at an extraordinary shareholders' meeting of Skandia on December 19. ($ = 6.642 Swedish Crowns)</p>
</text>
